The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
#include <asm/cpufeature.h>
#include <linux/jump_label.h>
#include <linux/atomic.h>
```
Reason:
The inclusion of `asm/cpufeature.h` brings in `linux/jump_label.h`, which requires `linux/atomic.h`. This creates a circular dependency with `asm/lse.h` and `asm/cpufeature.h` when `CC_HAVE_ASM_GOTO` is not defined, leading to compilation issues.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
#include <linux/stringify.h>
#include <asm/alternative.h>
```
Reason:
By moving the capability macros out of `asm/cpufeature.h` and adjusting the includes, the circular dependency is broken, allowing the code to compile correctly without the conflicting header inclusions.

